\begin{center}
\begin{minipage}{0.88\textwidth}
\small
\textbf{About this book.}\;
DSLtk is a header-only toolkit for constructing Domain-Specific Languages.
Its C++ implementation lives in a single file, \texttt{DSLtk.hpp}, and its D
port in a single module, \texttt{DSLtk.d}.  This book explains what those two
files contain, how the twenty-six feature tags fit together, how to
compose the facilities into a working language, and how to extend them.
Implementation descriptions refer to the supplied source snapshot.
Five case studies close the book, with companion executable programs.
\end{minipage}
\end{center}

